/// known-gap: interp has no tick() block or phase: blocks; the interpreter is being retired
/// An overlay's `phase: NAME` block holds spreads, `every N ticks` blocks
/// and transitions that run only in that phase of a `tick()` block; its
/// other lines run when the tick ends. Ageing and `lasts:` move once a
/// tick, at its end. A member of an overlay class gets the class's phases.
<>Town |
    n: 0
    sick: 0
    calm: 0
xx
overlay flu
    hosts: Town
    lasts: 3
    phase: spread
        spread: 1 where (target >> n) == (self >> n) + 1
        every 1 tick
            @sick |= @sick + 1
        xx
    xx
    every 1 tick
        @sick |= @sick + 10
    xx
xx
<^>Mood |
    hosts: Town
    phase: settle
        every 1 tick
            @calm |= @calm + 1
        xx
    xx
xx
overlay quiet <^> Mood
xx
a <> Town | n: 0
b <> Town | n: 1
c <> Town | n: 2
:overlay!(a, flu)
:overlay!(c, quiet)
repeat 4
    tick()
        spread
        settle
    xx
    on | :len(:overlays(flu))
    say("{a >> sick} {b >> sick} {c >> sick} flu on {on}, calm {c >> calm}")
xx
